As the above lines indicate, the segfault is occurring in the
PgSQLcloseConnection C function from the RdbiPgSQL package. Try re-
installing it and see if that helps. I have no experience with this
package, so it might even be a bug.

Also, check your R application code for dangling database connections.
The below line has me thinking that the Postgres connection is being
closed because a variable is going out of scope, R garbage collects
it, and then the finalizer kicks in to run cleanup.

