On Wed, Aug 8, 2012 at 3:05 PM, Jeffrey <jeffrey...@gmail.com> wrote:

> Hi Ken,
>
> Comments are inline below:
>
> On Aug 8, 4:05 pm, Ken Williams <ken.willi...@clearcapital.com> wrote:
> > We have some job submissions to an rApache program and about 20% of the
> > time these fail.
> > I've been troubleshooting this issue for a few days now and traced the
> > failures to segmentation faults in the httpd error_log.
> >
> > We're have the same issues on 5 nodes with identical configurations.
> >
> > I've been testing against a single node, and since I have updated to the
> > latest patch sets from CentOS5. I also updated R to 2.15.1 and compiled the
> > latest rapache as of 8/7/2012 via git.
> >
> > I've also gone as far as to install apache 2.2.22 from source tarball and
> > again, recompile rapache from source.
> >
> > I'm not sure if this is a code issue, and honestly I'm not an R developer
> > so I'm not sure how to make that determination. The R developer on staff
> > here has mentioned that running the same process via CLI (in absence of
> > rapache) the code executes fine and doesn't segfault. This leads me to
> > believe the issue is somewhere in rapache land...
> >
> > Any advice/assistance would be welcomed!
> >
> > Thanks,
> > -Ken Williams
